---
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en">
<head>
  <script is:inline>document.documentElement.classList.add('js');</script>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Privacy — disASTER</title>
  <meta name="description" content="What the disASTER newsletter collects (your email, if you subscribe), what it doesn't, and how to leave." />
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://dis-aster.vercel.app/privacy" />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Manrope:wght@400;500;700;800&family=Playfair+Display:ital@0;1&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
</head>

<body class="privacy-page">
  <a href="#main" class="skip-link">Skip to content</a>
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="privacy">
    <p class="privacy-kicker">Privacy</p>
    <h1>The short, honest version</h1>
    <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated 6 August 2026</p>

    <section>
      <h2>Who runs this</h2>
      <p>Damien Herlihy. Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:damienmunchip@gmail.com">damienmunchip@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What this site collects</h2>
      <p>One thing: your <strong>email address</strong>, and only if you type it into the subscribe form. It goes to <strong>Audienceful</strong>, the service that sends the newsletter. That's the entire list.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What this site doesn't do</h2>
      <p>No analytics. No trackers. No ads. This site sets no cookies of its own and stores nothing in your browser. Your data is never sold or shared.</p>
      <p>One footnote for completeness: the subscribe form's script comes from Audienceful's CDN, and its bot protection (Cloudflare) sets one short-lived cookie (<code>__cf_bm</code>, about 30 minutes) on Audienceful's own domain. It tells humans from bots; it doesn't track you across sites.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Fonts</h2>
      <p>The page loads its typefaces from Google Fonts, so that request goes to a Google server — which, like any web request, sees your IP address. No cookies are involved.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Leaving</h2>
      <p>Every email has an unsubscribe link. Unsubscribing removes you; if you want your address deleted entirely, email me and it's done.</p>
    </section>

    <footer class="privacy-foot">
      <a href="/">&larr; Back to disASTER</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
  <footer class="footer-whisper">
    <p>From Damien Herlihy — teacher, learner, maker.</p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>

<style>
  .privacy-page {
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: #000000;
  }

  .privacy {
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 72px var(--content-padding) 48px;
  }

  .privacy-kicker {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: var(--color-gold);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .privacy h1 {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 6vw, 44px);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .privacy-updated {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    color: var(--color-text-light);
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .privacy section {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .privacy h2 {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: var(--color-gold);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .privacy p {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .privacy a {
    color: var(--color-gold);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .privacy a:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid #ffffff;
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .privacy-foot {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .privacy-page .footer-whisper {
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 24px var(--content-padding) 36px;
    color: var(--color-text-light);
    font-size: 14px;
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
